The main saving is calling the virtual `GetType()` once instead of twice.

The function also replaces the general division with fast paths for element sizes of 1, 2, 4 and 8. It keeps ordinary division as a fallback for any other size, so results are unchanged. That fallback includes a size of 0, which divides by zero exactly as the original does.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
    {
        const size_t n = values.size();
        const size_t sz = baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK];
        switch (sz)
        {
            case 1: return (FIT_UINT8)n;
            case 2: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 1);
            case 4: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 2);
            case 8: return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 3);
            default: return (FIT_UINT8)(n / sz);
        }
    }

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```